# bsagent map-IP guard -- prepended to fw4's input_wan chain (priority before
# the ssh/web/bs_agent ACCEPTs) by the fw4 auto-include of
# /usr/share/nftables.d/chain-pre/<chain>/*.nft.
#
# Purpose: a configured bench Map IP (e.g. 10.0.96.169, a secondary IP on the
# wan interface) must NOT double as a router-management endpoint for arbitrary
# sources. The bench DNAT itself is already gated by the redirect's
# `option ipset allowed_bench_clients`, but a NON-allowlisted source can still
# reach the router's own sshd/uhttpd/bs_agent through the Map IP (the service
# ACCEPTs in input_wan are not destination-aware). This rule closes that gap:
# any ingress destined to a Map IP whose source is NOT in the allowlist is
# dropped, before those service ACCEPTs fire.
#
# Why input_wan and not the bench forward path: a DNAT'd flow has its daddr
# rewritten to the bench (192.168.1.x) in prerouting and is then FORWARDED --
# it never enters input_wan, so this rule cannot affect bench traffic. Only
# traffic that terminates on the router under a Map IP reaches here.
#
# @bench_map_ips   -- the set of live Map IPs (the src_dip of every enabled
#                     owned redirect). Its DEFINITION is always present via
#                     the table-pre include 30-bsagent-map-guard-set.nft, so
#                     this reference always resolves -- even before the
#                     uci-defaults migration runs (fail-safe: a missing config
#                     ipset section leaves the set EMPTY, not unresolved, so
#                     fw4 reload/restart never breaks). Its ENTRIES are seeded
#                     by the migration and kept current by benches.js
#                     syncMapIps().
# @allowed_bench_clients -- fw4 ipset; the client allowlist (same set the
#                     redirect DNAT gates on).
# Negated membership: ip saddr != @allowed_bench_clients. If the allowlist is
# empty, this is true for all sources (every Map IP is fully blocked); if it
# contains 0.0.0.0/0, it is false for all (the guard is a no-op). Exactly the
# complement of the redirect's `ip saddr @allowed_bench_clients` gate.
ip daddr @bench_map_ips ip saddr != @allowed_bench_clients counter drop comment "!bsagent: drop non-allowlisted ingress to map IP"
